  "stem": "\\[4x + 3y = 2\\] \\[2x - y = 6\\] If \\((x, y)\\) is the solution to the system of equations above, what is the value of \\(y\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "-2"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "From the second equation, \\(y = 2x - 6\\).",
    "Substitute: \\(4x + 3(2x - 6) = 2\\), so \\(10x - 18 = 2\\) and \\(x = 2\\).",
    "Then \\(y = 2(2) - 6 = -2\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x, y = symbols('x y')\nsol = solve([4*x + 3*y - 2, 2*x - y - 6], [x, y])\nassert sol == {x: 2, y: -2}\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == [sol[y]]",
